{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLCredit","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, a series of credit-words and credit-symbol elements within a single credit element follow one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another in sequence visually. Non-positional formatting attributes are carried over from the previous element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by default."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The page attribute for the credit element specifies the page number where the credit should appear. This is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integer value that starts with 1 for the first page. Its value is 1 by default. Since credits occur before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"music, these page numbers do not refer to the page numbering specified by the print element’s page-number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The credit-type element indicates the purpose behind a credit. Multiple types of data may be combined in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single credit, so multiple elements may be used. Standard values include page number, title, subtitle,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"composer, arranger, lyricist, rights, and part name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<credit>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcredit"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/init(id:kind:link:bookmark:content:page:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/bookmark","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/content-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/kind","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/link","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/page"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/Content-swift.enum"],"generated":true,"title":"Enumerations","anchor":"Enumerations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The credit type represents the appearance of the title, composer, arranger, lyricist, copyright, dedication,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and other text, symbols, and graphics that commonly appear on the first page of a score. The credit-words,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"credit-symbol, and credit-image elements are similar to the words, symbol, and image elements for directions.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, since the credit is not part of a measure, the default-x and default-y attri